{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/500110-the-new-vitakinesis-will-have-algesis","id":500110,"title":"The new Vitakinesis will have Algesis?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-02T03:33:01-07:00","id":500110,"title":"The new Vitakinesis will have Algesis?","content":"Reading the fantastic &quot;what we know so far&quot; ( <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ayGNCnAsHcgxIUr9k6mNYf46loqY8Qlv5v4TIImqgdU/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...gdU/edit?pli=1</a> ) from Chill i noticed that the new Vitakinesis psions will be more like Cap. America and i am wondering if the Algesis ability will be eliminated in the second edition; i hope not because it is really cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5811-starkiller","name":"Starkiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T07:14:23-07:00","id":500292,"title":"","content":"I doubt it. It seems the trend seems to swinging things up, rather than down, so we will see some physical enhancements but I doubt anything is going away. It also makes too much sense for them to as a power; after all, healing really is largely about controlled hurting: cutting things the right way, giving just enough of the right kind of poison, that kind of stuff. So I doubt Algesis is going anywhere. The general statement seems to be that the power system is going to shift, so we may no longer be stuck under three modes, specifically.<br /> <br /> Also while I would add that I have a theory: when it comes to game modifications, it's easier for the production side of things to add than to take away. Conversely, it's easier for the consumer/player side to delete rather than add. If I decide I don't want Clan Fischschlappe in my game because I feel they are ruining the mood or are overpowered or annoying or whatever, my group just says &quot;We aren't dealing with this shit&quot; and moves on. If Onyx Path wants to remove them, they usually have to come up with some kind of elaborate reason and deal with all the fan fallout from people who's Fischshlappe character was &quot;just the <i>best ever, you insensitive assholes</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> So I think overall during a redesign very little will be taken away so much as downplayed, and I don't think any existing abilities are going anywhere.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T09:28:09-07:00","id":500488,"title":"","content":"Furthermore, having an Aptitude that enables you to have some sort of psionic self-defense is at least kinda sorta maybe, y'know, <i>useful </i>in a war against superpowered human mutants. Take Algesis away from the vitakinetics and they're nothing more than two-legged, walking, talking, healing potions. Where's the fun in playing that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T08:02:06-07:00","id":509849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/500110-the-new-vitakinesis-will-have-algesis?p=500488#post500488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, having an Aptitude that enables you to have some sort of psionic self-defense is at least kinda sorta maybe, y'know, <i>useful </i>in a war against superpowered human mutants. Take Algesis away from the vitakinetics and they're nothing more than two-legged, walking, talking, healing potions. Where's the fun in playing that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it depends if you are diving into the &quot;War Against the Super Powered Mutants&quot; option entirely. The fun comes from the character, not necessarily just their powers, and I can have a lot of fun with characters who only have healing abilities, say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T09:23:24-07:00","id":509903,"title":"","content":"I can see both sides. The Doyen wanted the Psions to combat the Aberrants so they would make sure that all Psions were useful in that regard. That is from the thematic components, aka metaplot hammering down on you. However, I can easily see the appeal to playing a healer and only a healer. I am not the type to play someone who has no ability to layeth the smacketh down on the bad guys, but I know many players who enjoy playing a healing only cleric in D&amp;D or else some other support role. And every single one of my &quot;RAWR! KILL THE VILLAINS!&quot; guys have appreciated those other players. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T12:10:02-07:00","id":510088,"title":"","content":"What is this...&quot;healing only cleric in D&amp;D&quot; thingie you speak of? For that matter, what is this &quot;D&amp;D&quot; thing you speak of? Is it related to this pedestrian game of Dungeons &amp; Dragons that us tragically hip gamers who only play classic World of Darkness games occasionally hear about? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On a more serious note, a healing-only character never really appealed to me either, but every decent gaming group recognizes the necessity of the cleric or genre-appropriate equivalent healer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T14:55:40-07:00","id":510206,"title":"","content":"When I play D&amp;D 4th edition I mostly play the support characters because in 4th edition they are total badasses. Plus I like to spend a long time looking for the funky, quirky or plain broken combos and by loading up on those on a Leader in 4th Edition I basically make everyone else in the group better so I can 'powergame' to my hearts content while not overshadowing everyone else...in fact often making everyone else better and more fun to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T16:14:59-07:00","id":510223,"title":"","content":"I just enjoy several characters where loading them down with offensive options would be inappropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T18:15:34-07:00","id":510275,"title":"","content":"Ewwwwwwwwww...4th Edition. Shun the non-believer. SHUUUUUUUUUN!<br /> lol<br /> In all seriousness, whatever works for you and your table is how things go. If you enjoy that, great. Like I said, I like to play someone who can bring the pain. I have a friend who, no matter the game or the system, he was my BBB. Best Buff Buddy. Before I charged into a fight, he would like to stack as many buffs as he could on me and then let me do my thing. Which is why I think the new version of vitakinesis will be tremendously awesome. The addition of Algesis will also help things out to make sure that an Aesculapian would be cool to have in a group. They can help people out and, when cornered? Go &quot;Suck on this: Sci-fi version of HARM!&quot; and then run back to their Legionnaire and Orgotek pals who are blasting the crud out of the mongrel Aberrant hordes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T20:35:24-07:00","id":516683,"title":"","content":"My vitakinetic faith healer preacher would say we wouldn't need to abuse our heavenly gifts for violence; that is why the Lord gave us guns: to protect us from the Aberrants and homosexual dinosaurs after we were cast from Eden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T22:18:38-07:00","id":516763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/500110-the-new-vitakinesis-will-have-algesis?p=516683#post516683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My vitakinetic faith healer preacher would say we wouldn't need to abuse our heavenly gifts for violence; that is why the Lord gave us guns: to protect us from the Aberrants and homosexual dinosaurs after we were cast from Eden.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, judging from Divis Mal's example, I thought Aberrants <i>were </i>homosexual dinosaurs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}